    "q-347264": {
      "dom_id": "step-q347264",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "A factory spends  $C(x)=0.002375{x}^{2}+0.3x+1\\,000$ dollars to manufacture $x$ units of a certain product. The factory sells the product for $30-\\frac{x}{100}$ dollars per unit. Given that the factory can produce at most $2\\,000$ units per year, how many units should the factory produce per year to maximize its annual profit?\n\nThe optimal number of production is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we apply the candidates test.\n\nFirst, note that for selling $x$ units of the product per year, the factory has an annual revenue (income) of $R(x)=(30-\\frac{x}{100})\\cdot x=30x-0.01{x}^{2}$ dollars.\n\nTherefore, the profit function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =R(x)-C(x) \\\\  & =30x-0.01{x}^{2}-(0.002375{x}^{2}+0.3x+1\\,000) \\\\  & =-1\\,000+29.7x-0.012375{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe note that the permitted domain is $0\\le x\\le 2\\,000.$\n\nWe need to find the critical points of $P(x)$ for $0<x<2\\,000.$ Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(x)=29.7-0.02475x.\n$$\n\nSolving ${P}^{′}(x)=0$ gives the following critical point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 29.7-0.02475x & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $x=1\\,200$ lies in the interval $0<x<2\\,000.$ All that's left now is to confirm that $x=1\\,200$ does indeed give a maximum value of $P(x).$ To do this, we compute the second derivative:   \n\n$$\n{P}^{″}(x)=-0.02475<0.\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, the point $x=1\\,200$ is indeed a  maximum of $P(x).$ \n\nOur candidates are $x=0,$ $x=1\\,200,$ and $x=2\\,000.$ Computing $P(x)$ at each of these values, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =-1\\,000 \\\\ P(1\\,200) & =-1\\,000+29.7(1\\,200)-0.012375(1\\,200)^{2}=16\\,820\\,✓ \\\\ P(2\\,000) & =-1\\,000+29.7(2\\,000)-0.012375(2\\,000)^{2}=9\\,500\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the factory will have a maximum annual profit when it produces $1\\,200$ units per year.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
